WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.983
- Hey guys, it's Justine,

00:00:00.983 --> 00:00:02.870
and we are at the Samsung
Galaxy Unpacked event

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.570
and guess what we have here?

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.100
This is the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.830
They announced this before
the event even happened

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.950
and they aired a commercial at the Oscars,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.890
which was kind of incredible
because there were rumors,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.770
but the Oscars commercial
just confirmed it.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:17.863
And here it is, it's in my hands.

00:00:19.007 --> 00:00:21.590
(gentle music)

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.840
So this is the Z Flip.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.680
It has a 6.7-inch AMOLED
Infinity Flex display

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.380
with a 1.1-inch AMOLED
display on the front.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.730
When you double-tap on the power button,

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.890
which also is a fingerprint sensor,

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.340
this will activate the selfie camera,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.490
so you can take a selfie.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.323
Look at that!

00:00:41.323 --> 00:00:42.450
It also has wireless charging,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.240
but it isn't 5G compatible
with the rest of the S20s.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.310
It's running a Snapdragon 855 Plus.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.740
It has eight gigs of
RAM, 256 gigs of storage,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.860
and 3300 milliamp dual battery.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.240
There's two 12 megapixel
cameras in the back.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.250
There's a wide angle
and an ultra-wide angle

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.330
and on the inside, of course,
it has a selfie camera,

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.740
and that's 10 megapixels.

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.440
It comes in three different colors.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.860
There's mirror purple, black,
and gold in some markets.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.970
They also have one other version.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.900
This is the Thom Browne edition.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.810
This one is a limited edition version

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.440
and they are launching it
at New York Fashion Week.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.715
So I only get a few
minutes with this thing,

00:01:13.715 --> 00:01:14.830
but what the crazy part about this

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.090
is this is being released
on Valentine's Day,

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.460
so what a treat to us.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.790
You can get it at various retailers and

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.700
the fact that this is
being launched so soon

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.040
without pre-orders or
anything was kind of shocking.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.380
When I saw that flash up on the screen,

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.500
I was like, "wait a minute,
that's just a few days away."

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.070
So my initial impressions
is it doesn't feel cheap

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.840
like I feel like one of the things that

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.370
when you have a flip phone like this

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.000
I never really had much time
with the Samsung Galaxy Fold

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.330
but one of the things I like about this is

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.100
this feels substantial,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.400
like when this is in my hand, like,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.930
it feels nice.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.193
Let me do a pocket test.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.970
This isn't a real pocket!

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.403
What kind of lie is this?

00:01:52.403 --> 00:01:53.236
- [Jenna] You want to put it in my pocket?

00:01:53.236 --> 00:01:54.650
- Do you have a pocket?
- I have a pocket.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:57.300
- [Justine] In Jenna's pocket,
'cause I don't have one.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.720
That's nice.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.370
Oh, flex.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.260
That's cool.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.383
Give me that back!

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.120
So what's cool about this
is different applications

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.120
will change depending upon
how you have the phone.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.850
So right now we have the full screen mode,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.450
we're watching YouTube,
but if we fold this,

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.620
the video will continue to play up top,

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.980
but down below you have all
of your YouTube comments

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.780
and you can basically interact with this

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.423
like a little tiny laptop.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:23.970
It's so cute!

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.540
You can also do full screen mode.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.373
Ta-da!

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.700
So one of the things I
really like is this hinge.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.910
It's really stiff so if you
were to place this somewhere,

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.490
it can basically kind of
act as a little tripod.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.470
They did a little demo
at the Keynote where

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:41.660
you can take a selfie or
you can do Google Duo calls.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.760
I like this because it doesn't feel

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.180
like it's just gonna shut on it's own

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.260
and speaking of closing it.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.830
You have over 200,000 folds, they say.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.200
You can tell that there is
a little bit of a crease,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.950
but this doesn't feel like plastic

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.030
because it's actually a
very, very ultra-thin glass.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.863
Do you see me?

00:02:57.863 --> 00:02:58.696
Do you see it?

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.670
I just took our picture
using the front flip.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.503
How cool!

00:03:04.503 --> 00:03:07.320
So this is just my first look
at the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.153
This is pretty cool.

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.210
I love the future thoughts of

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.520
the integration of having
foldable phones like this

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.290
because taking something that is this big,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.210
folding it in half, and
it is now half the size,

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.560
I am definitely really into that.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.610
I was gonna say that I wish I
could do that with my laptop,

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.310
but technically that's kind
of what you're already doing.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.143
Well, see you guys later.

00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:27.590
I'll have some more
videos coming out soon.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:29.130
So make sure you like,
comment, and subscribe!

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.130
Make sure to hit the bell

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.340
and I will see you in my next video.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:32.173
Jenna, your turn.

00:03:32.173 --> 00:03:33.006
- [Jenna] Thank you!

00:03:33.006 --> 00:03:35.390
- Oh, I need a thumbnail!

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.460
- Did you see what colors it comes in?

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:38.943
- Yeah, in the VO.

00:03:38.943 --> 00:03:42.276
(slow electronic music)

